# Development Guide - Tauri AI Computer Use Agent ✅

## Critical Development Requirements

### Mandatory Compilation Check
**ALWAYS run after ANY Rust code changes**:
```bash
cargo check --manifest-path src-tauri/Cargo.toml
```
- Must complete with exit code 0 before considering changes complete
- Address all compiler errors and warnings immediately
- Do not loop more than 3 times on fixing linter errors for the same file

### File Organization Standards
- Keep files under 700 lines when possible
- Check for existing files before creating new ones to avoid redundancy
- Use workspace-relative imports (`crate::`) consistently
- Follow the existing modular structure in [src-tauri/src/](mdc:src-tauri/src)

## Development Patterns

### State Management Pattern
All persistent state flows through [src-tauri/src/state.rs](mdc:src-tauri/src/state.rs):

```rust
// Access state in commands
#[tauri::command]
async fn my_command(app_state: tauri::State<'_, AppState>) -> Result<String, String> {
    let desktop = &app_state.desktop;
    // Use centralized state
}
```

### Tool Implementation Pattern
All tools follow this async pattern:

```rust
let tool_exec = move |input: Value| {
    let app_handle = app_handle_clone.clone();
    async move {
        let state_manager = app_handle.state::<AppState>();

        // Parse input
        let args = serde_json::from_value::<InputStruct>(input)
            .map_err(|e| format!("Failed to parse input: {}", e))?;

        // Execute operation with proper error handling
        match state_manager.desktop.operation(args) {
            Ok(result) => Ok(json!({"success": true, "data": result})),
            Err(e) => Err(format!("Operation failed: {}", e))
        }
    }
};
```

### Event System Pattern
Use Tauri events for backend→frontend communication:

```rust
// Backend event emission
if let Err(e) = app_handle.emit("event-name", payload) {
    tracing::error!("Failed to emit event: {}", e);
}
```

```typescript
// Frontend event listening
useEffect(() => {
    const setupListeners = async () => {
        const unlisten = await listen<PayloadType>("event-name", (event) => {
            // Handle event
        });
        return unlisten;
    };

    const cleanup = setupListeners();
    return () => {
        cleanup?.then(unlisten => unlisten?.());
    };
}, []);
```

